Package: backgammonr
Type: Package
Title: Finite-Budget Rollout Allocation for Backgammon
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Gabriel",
           family = "Alwan",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gabriel.alwan@gmail.com")
Author: Gabriel Alwan [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gabriel Alwan <gabriel.alwan@gmail.com>
Description: Research-oriented statistical-computing tools for finite-budget
    simulation allocation in backgammon. The package frames a board state plus
    realized dice roll as a ranking-and-selection problem under Monte Carlo
    noise and centers Thompson sampling and related allocation rules for
    best-action identification. It combines a C++ backgammon engine, rollout
    value estimation, high-budget reference approximation, baseline comparison
    methods, benchmarking helpers, and reporting tools for probability of
    correct selection, simple regret, value-estimation error, and runtime
    tradeoffs.
